[Music]  what's the latest diet trend this year  that can help me lose weight  does this sound familiar  every year  new fat diets pop up with promises that  drastically changing your diet can help  you lose sweet but in reality this type  of quick fix weight loss doesn't last  how many of you have been on a diet how  many times have you failed let me know  in the comments below  if you really want to go on a diet and  drop the pounds for good your best bet  is to adopt healthy habits that you will  be able to maintain over the long term  so ask yourself these questions before  settling on a new diet  is this diet sustainable for me meaning  can you do it 7 days a week or forever  is this diet overly restrictive if you  are going to feel deprived well  trust me it will be tough to stick to it  because eventually those cravings will  take over  will you be able to live your life while  on it that means will you be able to  have a social life and still enjoy meals  out with your family and friends will  you be adequately nourished this is the  most important question to ask yourself  if you're restricting and depriving your  body of the nutrient it needs to  function it's going to do more harm than  good just keep this in mind the best  diet is the one that doesn't feel like a  diet the plant incorporates all food  groups teaches you about portion sizes  and provides healthy cooking tips in  fact the best diet is actually not a  diet but a lifestyle which you can  sustain forever  so  after going through an endless list of  diets here are my top three best diets  which have been scientifically proven to  help you lose weight and maintain a  healthy weight for life i'll be sharing  with you the food portions and how you  can easily incorporate them into your  daily life  a healthy balanced diet means eating a  variety of foods from each major food  group from proteins and carbohydrates to  fruits and vegetables even if you're in  good health you should still avoid  highly processed foods and added sugars  so a typical healthy balanced macro  breakdown would be 50 carbs 30 fat and  20 protein to keep it simple your  healthy plate should look like this  half vegetables quarter protein and  quarter cups so aim to fill your plate  with a variety of colorful vegetables as  they are a great source of vitamins  minerals antioxidants and dietary fiber  so aim to consume two to three servings  of vegetables in each meal here's what a  serving of vegetables looks like  one cup of raw leafy greens such as  spinach or lettuce half a cup of chunky  vegetables such as broccoli florets bell  peppers and carrots or  half a cup of vegetable juice you can  also add a piece of fruit to your meal  or  simply have it as a snack  as for protein choose high quality  proteins such as chicken breasts fish  meat tempeh tofu beans and legumes so  the general recommendation is about 0.8  grams of protein per kilo of your body  weight but if you lead an active  lifestyle then consume between 1.2 to  1.7 grams of protein per kilo of your  body weight for example if you weigh 54  kilos and you consume about 1.5 grams of  protein per kilo of your body weight  that means you should be consuming about  81 grams of protein in a day  so how you can achieve that is to  consume two eggs for breakfast  one portion of salmon for lunch  half a cup of greek yogurt as your snack  and one portion of white fish for dinner  this gives you a total of 81 grams of  protein so protein is extremely  important to repair and build muscle  tissue transport and store nutrients and  coordinate bodily functions  as for carbohydrates choose healthy  complex cups such as rice quinoa oats  buckwheat noodles sweet potatoes pumpkin  whole grain pasta or wholemeal bread  the main function of carbohydrate is to  provide your body with energy for  example if you consume 1 800 calories a  day and 50 of that is carbs that means  your daily cup intake is about 225 grams  and how you can simply achieve that is  to consume two slices of bread for  breakfast  one small bowl of rice for lunch one  small bowl of rice for dinner  a banana as your snack  a medium baked sweet potato  and  not forgetting your five servings of  vegetables that gives you a total of 220  grams of carbs in a day and as for  healthy fats you can easily integrate  them into your diet by using olive oil  in your cooking and consuming oily fish  peanut butter avocado nuts and seeds  healthy fats keep the heart healthy  protect your organs and support cell  growth and provide energy  so here's what one serving of healthy  fats look like one tablespoon of oil or  butter one ounce of nuts half an avocado  and fats from 4 ounces of salmon fillet  now remember to consume them in small  quantities as they are calorie dense so  this is a general guideline for the  healthy balanced diet the goal here is  to consume a wide variety of foods in  moderation by keeping to your daily  calorie needs and macros and of course  you can still enjoy your occasional  treats of processed foods and desserts  but keep them in small quantities  remember the key here is balance and  moderation  this next diet has been voted as the  best diet year after year it is the  mediterranean diet so what's the  mediterranean diet and why is it so  popular and effective for weight loss  the mediterranean diet incorporates the  traditional healthy living habits of  people from the mediterranean region so  this diet is essentially low in carbs  low in saturated fats and high in  unsaturated fats it puts a higher focus  on plant foods and cooking using healthy  fats such as olive oil with plenty of  flavorful spices  so following this diet can improve  healthy cholesterol levels and keep  blood sugar levels in a healthy range  now remember there's no one right method  to follow the mediterranean diet but  here are some basic rules you can start  with consume a wide variety of  vegetables fruits whole grains beans  nuts  herbs spices and unsaturated fats such  as olive oil daily consume fish and  other seafood twice weekly consume a  moderate portion of poultry eggs cheese  yogurt  as well as red wine and only  occasionally consume red meat and sweets  so a general portion breakdown for this  diet will consist of 50 cups  35 to 40 fats and 15 to 20 protein so  people following this diet would either  limit or avoid their consumption of  refined grains refined oil added sugars  sugar-sweetened beverages  processed meats and other highly  processed foods  the mediterranean diet believes that  whole single ingredient foods are often  crucial to good health therefore to  start building your own mediterranean  diet recipes you'll want to stock up on  whole grains such as whole oats brown  rice rye bread barley buckwheat and  whole grain pasta tubers such as  potatoes sweet potatoes and yams  vegetables such as lettuce spinach  onions broccoli carrots and cucumber  fruits such as tomatoes apples bananas  nectarines strawberries dragon fruit and  dates  nuts and seeds which includes almonds  cashews walnuts sunflower seeds and  pumpkin seeds  legumes which includes beans lentils  peas  pulses and chickpeas  seafood such as salmon mackerel white  fish shrimp and shellfish poultry such  as chicken and eggs healthy fats such as  olives olive oil and avocados dairy such  as greek yogurt milk and cheese and  finally herbs and spices so the  mediterranean way of eating is generally  rich in healthy plant foods and  relatively low in animal products and  meats with a focus on fish and seafood  so following this diet long term can  improve your weight and prevent certain  health issues such as heart disease  stroke and type 2 diabetes  and the final best diet for weight  management is the low carb diet this  diet limits your cup intake which  encourages your body to use more fat as  fuel  if you know that you have a higher  sensitivity towards cups and your body  has a higher resistance to insulin then  the low carb diet may work well for you  insulin is the hormone responsible for  controlling your blood sugar levels so a  high level of insulin resistance means  that your blood sugar levels are likely  to spike after consuming cups especially  refined cups  so some of the common signs of carb  sensitivity include intense craving for  refined cups  struggling with always feeling hungry  which can lead to overeating energy  level dips after an hour of consuming  cups you tend to gain weight easily  and you experience cup withdrawal  symptoms such as headaches irritability  mood swings and anxiety carb sensitivity  is a real thing and it just might be the  reason why weight loss can be  challenging for you  now if you fall under this category it  doesn't mean that you cannot consume  carbs at all but you need to choose the  good cups and limit your portion  your goal is to choose non-starchy  colorful vegetables high quality  proteins and healthy fats  let's first understand what are carbs  carbs are an essential part of a healthy  diet however it is very important to  know that not all cups are created equal  so how then do we differentiate between  good carbs and bad cups  good cups are complex cups which are  unprocessed and contain fiber found  naturally in food  so these examples include quinoa oats  buckwheat noodle brown rice sweet  potatoes pumpkin and beans they are  loaded with nutrients and fiber and  provide sustained energy on the other  hand  bad cups are refined cups which have  been processed and had the natural fiber  removed or changed examples include  cereal cakes pastries biscuits pizza  sodas and added sugars they are usually  lacking in nutrients hence they are  referred to as empty calories so our  bodies process refined cups quickly and  they do not provide lasting energy and  this can cause a spike in blood sugar  levels and the goal here is to reduce or  avoid all refined carbs in your diet  so a low carb diet macro breakdown would  be 15 to 25 cups 40 to 50 protein  and 25 to 30 fat  you want to limit your cup intake to  about 100 to 150 grams per day and the  key here is to limit starchy cups and  aim to consume more non-starchy cups so  aim to consume only about two to three  servings of starchy cups in a day so for  example half a cup of oats for breakfast  1 small bowl of cooked brown rice for  lunch and around 150 grams of sweet  potatoes for dinner on the other hand  you can increase your protein portion to  2 servings in each meal so for example  you can have cheesy tuna omelette for  breakfast  2 portions of chicken breast for lunch  2 servings of fish for dinner and 1 cup  of greek yogurt topped with nuts and  seeds as your snack so having a high  protein diet will keep you full for  longer stabilize your blood sugar levels  and reduce cravings as for healthy fats  again you can easily integrate them into  your diet by using olive oil in your  cooking and consuming oily fish peanut  butter avocado nuts and seeds  healthy fats keep the heart healthy  protect your organs support cell growth  and provide energy so when you are carb  sensitive consuming carb rich foods has  a greater impact on your overall  well-being than merely reducing your  calorie intake therefore you need to pay  more attention to the types of carbs you  consume  just know that diets aren't just for  weight loss while changing your diet can  be one of the best ways to lose weight  it can also be a gateway to improving  your habits focusing on your health and  leading a more active lifestyle  although the three diets have been shown  to be effective for weight loss the diet  you choose should depend on your  lifestyle and food preferences  this will ensure that you are more  likely to stick to it in the long term  now remember this is just a guideline  for you to understand each diet before  starting any new kind of diet it is  always a good idea to talk with your  doctor about your personal health  history they can always help you decide  which plan would work best for you so  let me know which is your preferred diet  in the comments below and don't forget  to give this video a thumbs up and share  it on with your friends as well okay  and what other topics would you like to  learn more of let me know in the  comments below don't forget to also hit  the subscribe button if you haven't yet  done it go on to my channel to learn  more about healthy food recipes as well  as check out a lot more workout videos  and mindset tips and i will see you next  time all the best

